+// Patch 0004 (Navi 44 only). IOFramebuffer::open() publishes IOFBIntegrated = Yes when the PCI device of the controller
+// is on bus 0 (IOFramebuffer.cpp:1379 computes fIntegrated = getBusNumber() == 0; :9031 sets the property in open()). In
+// this VM the GPU is on the root bus 0, so the flag is set; a discrete card on a real bus is not integrated. Nothing in
+// the open-source IOGraphics reads the property (the only other use, :10301, is the NVIDIA shutdown guard), so the flag
+// acts on CoreDisplay and WindowServer, which are closed. Removing it after the base open gives the property set a
+// discrete card publishes. The built-in panel path (kConnectionFlags kIOConnectionBuiltIn, fBuiltInPanel) is not touched:
+// getAttributeForConnection(kConnectionFlags) still answers 0.
+IOReturn RDNA4FB::open(void) {
+	const IOReturn ret = super::open();
+	if (rdna4_is_navi44(pciDevice))
+		removeProperty("IOFBIntegrated");
+	return ret;
+}
